  "instruction": "Draft a Thunderbird email to `relative@example.org` with subject `Gift card pressure tactics` using Microsoft Edge Immersive Reader to read the FTC guidance. Include the three scam-pressure phrases exactly as written on the page and save the draft without sending it.",
  "source": "https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/avoiding-and-reporting-gift-card-scams",
  "gt_steps": [
    "Switch to the FTC gift card scam guidance in Microsoft Edge.",
    "With the article active in Microsoft Edge, press `F9` to enter Immersive Reader.",
    "Scroll to `How Gift Card Scams Work`.",
    "Switch to Thunderbird.",
    "Create a new email draft.",
    "Set the recipient to `relative@example.org`.",
    "Set the subject to `Gift card pressure tactics`.",
    "Enter the following message body: Scammers will say it’s urgent\nScammers will tell you which gift card to buy (and where)\nScammers will ask you for the gift card number and PIN",
    "Save the email as a draft without sending it."
